  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_036: multimodal, scvi_n200, ViT-L, avgpool, concat; acc=0.715) establishes that multimodal fusion with scvi_n200 and ViT-L is the strongest direction. However, we only have one aggregation test in the multimodal setting (avgpool). In the RNA-only setting, aggregation choice was a major factor (avgpool 0.591 vs transformer 0.519 for PCA), but this has not been validated in the multimodal regime where the interaction between image features and RNA features may alter the optimal aggregation strategy. Config_038 (multimodal, scvi_n200, ViT-L, transformer, concat) is a minimal, controlled change from config_036 that directly tests whether transformer aggregation can outperform avgpool when both modalities are present. If transformer underperforms, it confirms avgpool as the robust choice and lets us focus remaining budget on other dimensions (e.g., RNA encoder or image encoder). If transformer outperforms, it reveals a new promising direction. This is the highest-information experiment because it resolves a key architectural uncertainty in the currently best-performing family with a single clean comparison."
}

